/* The layout of app.py, and none of its behaviour.

   This is a real stylesheet -- Textual parses CSS. What it means is that the
   arrangement of the interface is data in a file, not a sequence of .pack() calls
   inside __init__ as it was in module 24. You can change the width of the table
   here and restart, and no Python was touched.

   Textual's dialect is small and mostly self-explanatory. The units that are not:
   `1fr` is one share of the remaining space, and `auto` is as much as the content
   needs. */

#title {
    padding: 0 1;
    background: $accent;
    color: $text;
    text-style: bold;
}

#controls {
    height: auto;
    padding: 1;
}

#controls Label {
    padding: 1 1 0 0;
}

#limit {
    width: 12;
}

#table {
    height: 1fr;
    border: round $primary;
}

#status {
    height: auto;
    padding: 0 1;
    color: $text-muted;
}
